• Findings:

  - `scripts/land/install-bot.sh:41` — a fresh clone logs `INSTALL_ORIGIN_URL` verbatim, leaking any URL credentials despite the new redaction elsewhere. Fix by piping `ORIGIN_URL` through `redact` in this message too. Add a fresh-clone test with credentialed input and assert that no userinfo appears.

  - `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh:575` — the stale gate-clone test checks only the exit status and diagnostic. It would still pass if the transport fetched first and checked the origin afterward, contrary to its “before it fetches” claim. Fix by instrumenting host-side `git fetch` and asserting that the log remains empty.

  - `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh:681` — the credential-redaction test exercises the train, pre-push hook, helper, and installer’s extracted sed expression, but never executes `push-both.sh`. Thus the changed output at `scripts/push-both.sh:90` can regress unnoticed. Fix by invoking `push-both.sh` with a canonical credentialed URL and a git shim that stops before network access, then assert redaction and absence of the complete userinfo.

  The transport guard itself is correctly ordered before fetching, both redaction implementations handle the authority’s last `@`, and the underscore alias change is sound. Changed shell scripts pass `bash -n`; no additional Bash 3.2/BSD portability or whole-branch migration defects found.

  VERDICT: REJECT
